member.summary:
As ;
 is true for a real crossing (each triangle has corners strictly on both sides of
the other's plane) and false when they only touch (an edge or corner lying on the other's face).

The bookmark tour's settings (tour round), saved with the bookmarks (inside a .bimgo, or in the live model
folder). Each bookmark can override the hold and swivel (,
) or be left out ().

Round K-C: a sun time part way between two others (the tour and camera paths animate the sun with it). The date
moves the short way round the year (December → January goes through New Year, not back through the whole year);
the clock time moves straight from one to the other; daylight saving switches halfway.

            What a sync does:


a wanted marker already in the model is updated (values) and moved (point) where they differ;

one not in the model is placed, unless BimGo placed it before (it was deleted in Revit: left out until
            );

with , markers of comments not in the list are removed; with
            , closed comments' markers are removed and not placed.

            A marker BimGo removes is forgotten (placed again if its comment comes back or reopens); a deleted one stays
            remembered. Markers without an id (placed by hand) and second copies of an id are left alone.

Round Y-C1: the file's output factor for a lamp tilted this far from how it was measured (degrees: for a
fixture, how far its aim is turned from straight down). Linear between the file's angles, held at its ends;
1 without tilt data. LM-63 applies it to every candela value, so it scales the output, not the shape.

            Materials and textures captured at extraction (optional: only when "Extract materials and textures" was ticked
            at Go / Export). Drives the walkthrough's Realistic colour mode:


a material table (render colour, texture, real-world placement, glass reflectivity);

a per-vertex material index ( = the vertex keeps its baked colour);

per-vertex surface coordinates in metres along each face's own axes (Revit-like alignment);

the texture images, re-encoded and size-capped, keyed by their entry name in the .bimgo.

            Older files and light extractions have none ().

Loads the overrides kept in a model's BimGo folder (texture-overrides.json, see
). With no folder, uses the per-key file in .
Never throws.
